{
  "summary": "Replaces outbound full-relay peers that decline transaction relay with peers that do, active only outside of initial block download and non-blocksonly mode. The node establishes an extra outbound connection before evicting the non-relaying peer to prevent dipping below the target connection count, and strips chain-sync eviction protection from non-relaying peers unless they are the sole connection on a network. It also renames ForEachNode to ForEachFullyConnectedNode to reflect its built-in filtering.",
  "problem": "Outbound full-relay slots can be consumed by peers that do not relay transactions (such as nodes running with -blocksonly). When this happens, a node's transaction relay topology and diversity degrade without the operator's knowledge, potentially leaving the node with too few peers to reliably broadcast or receive unconfirmed transactions.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Outbound-full-relay slots should be used by peers that actually relay transactions, besides #28538 see #16418 and #28371 for the motivation.'",
    "Linked issue #16418 ('Ensure we have sufficient transaction-relay peers') and #28371 ('Seek more/different peers when ours all have too high feefilter') document how nodes can get starved of tx-relay capacity by passive or high-feefilter peers."
