  "card": "Replaces outbound full-relay peers that do not relay transactions with peers that do, ensuring nodes maintain sufficient transaction relay capacity and network diversity. To avoid dropping below outbound connection targets, an extra outbound connection is established before evicting a non-relaying peer, and non-relaying peers are denied disconnect protection unless they are the only connection on a given network. The replacement mechanism is disabled during initial block download and when running with -blocksonly. This addresses issues #16418 and #28371, redesigning the approach from closed PR #28538 to connect replacements prior to eviction.",
